  <section id="descent">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>1. Dynamical Descent, Output-Null Fibers &amp; Intrinsic Manifolds</h2>
      <span class="mod-tag">neuro/descent.cub</span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <span>Interactive Manifold &amp; Output-Null Fiber Lab</span>
          <span id="manStatus" class="badge ok">WITHIN-MANIFOLD · REACHABLE</span>
        </div>
        <canvas id="manCanvas"></canvas>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <button class="btn on" id="btnManWithin">Within-Manifold Decoder</button>
          <button class="btn" id="btnManOut">Outside-Manifold Decoder</button>
        </div>
        <div class="ctrl">
          <label>Target y <input type="range" id="manTarget" min="-100" max="100" value="55"><span id="manTargetVal">0.55</span></label>
          <label>Null fiber <input type="range" id="manNull" min="-100" max="100" value="35"><span id="manNullVal">0.35</span></label>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="thm"><b>descent-preserves-fiber / fiber-preserved-descends</b> — A macro-law \(g : O \to O\) descends through an observation \(o : S \to O\) iff \(T\) preserves the fibers of \(o\).</div>
        <p><b>Output-null vs. output-potent (Kaufman et al., 2014):</b> Motor preparation moves neural state along the pink line \(\mathsf{Fib}_o(y)\) without changing behavioral output \(y\) (<code>null-preserves-output</code>). Drag the <i>Null fiber</i> slider: the neural point moves while the decoded readout stays pinned.</p>
        <p><b>Intrinsic manifold (Sadtler et al., 2014):</b> Neural activity is confined to the blue intrinsic submanifold \(M \hookrightarrow S\). A within-manifold perturbation transports reachability via an equivalence \(e : M \simeq M\) (<code>within-manifold-reach</code>). Switch to <i>Outside-Manifold</i>: the target fiber \(\mathsf{Fib}_{d'}(y)\) misses \(M\) completely (<code>outside-manifold-impossible</code>).</p>
        <pre>null-preserves-output : (o : S → O) → (f : NullDynamics o)
  → (s : S) → o (run-null o f s) ≡ o s
non-ergodic-no-pop-law : (g : Nat → Nat)
  → Descends pop-sum ens-step g → Empty</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="coproc">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>2. Two-Learner Neural Co-Processors: SOS Stability &amp; Control Barrier Safety</h2>
      <span class="mod-tag">neuro/lyapunov.cub · neuro/barrier.cub · neuro/coproc.cub · neuro/reshaping-coproc.cub</span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <span>2-Learner Phase Plane &amp; CBF Safe Ball (Click to launch trajectory)</span>
          <span id="cpStatus" class="badge ok">SOS STABLE · CBF SAFE</span>
        </div>
        <canvas id="cpCanvas"></canvas>
        <div class="ctrl">
          <label>Brain η_B <input type="range" id="cpEb" min="5" max="40" value="20"><span id="cpEbVal">2.0</span></label>
          <label>Decoder η_C <input type="range" id="cpEc" min="5" max="40" value="25"><span id="cpEcVal">2.5</span></label>
          <label>Coupling γ <input type="range" id="cpGm" min="0" max="40" value="12"><span id="cpGmVal">1.2</span></label>
          <label>CBF rate α <input type="range" id="cpAl" min="2" max="30" value="10"><span id="cpAlVal">1.0</span></label>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="thm"><b>two-learner-sym-sos-id &amp; cbf-2learner-safe-sos-id</b> — Universal polynomial SOS identities over \(\mathbb{Q}\) certifying global stability (\(\eta_B \eta_C > \gamma^2\)) and Control Barrier forward-invariance of \(h(e) = R^2 - e_B^2 - e_C^2 \ge 0\) whenever \((2\eta_B - \alpha)(2\eta_C - \alpha) \ge 4\gamma^2\).</div>
        <p>In a closed-loop neural co-processor (Rao 2019; Carmena; Madduri–Burden–Orsborn 2023), brain error \(e_B\) and decoder error \(e_C\) co-adapt: \(\dot{e}_B = -\eta_B e_B + \gamma e_C,\; \dot{e}_C = \gamma e_B - \eta_C e_C\). Drag \(\gamma\) above \(\sqrt{\eta_B \eta_C}\) to watch the saddle instability tear trajectories out of the safe ball.</p>
        <p><b>Proof-gated activation (`SafeGateDS` in `neuro/reshaping-coproc.cub`):</b> Unlike Kunz et al.'s surface lexical password (refuted by <code>lexical-gate-fails</code>), switching from probing mode to active coupled mode requires an explicit <code>SafeAt</code> / <code>Warranted</code> proof witness—while <code>safe-off-switch</code> decouples unconditionally.</p>
        <pre>-- Certified over every commutative ring containing Q (al-id)
two-learner-sym-sos-id : al-id 5 two-learner-sym-sos ≡ true
cbf-2learner-safe-sos-id : al-id 7 cbf-2learner-safe-sos ≡ true
lexical-gate-fails : Neg (SafeAt (λ s → fst s) true (λ s → snd s ≡ true))</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="excitable">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>3. Externally Driven FitzHugh–Nagumo Excitable Membrane</h2>
      <span class="mod-tag">neuro/barrier.cub · fhn-driven-trapping-sos-id</span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <span>FHN Phase Plane &amp; Machine-Checked Trapping Region</span>
          <span id="fhnStatus" class="badge ok">TRAPPED · SOS CERTIFIED</span>
        </div>
        <canvas id="fhnCanvas"></canvas>
        <div class="ctrl">
          <label>Drive I <input type="range" id="fhnI" min="-150" max="150" value="50"><span id="fhnIVal">0.50</span></label>
          <label>Offset a <input type="range" id="fhnA" min="-100" max="100" value="70"><span id="fhnAVal">0.70</span></label>
          <label>Damping b <input type="range" id="fhnB" min="20" max="150" value="80"><span id="fhnBVal">0.80</span></label>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="thm"><b>fhn-driven-trapping-sos-id</b> — For \(\dot{v} = v - \frac{1}{3}v^3 - w + I,\; \dot{w} = \varepsilon(v + a - bw)\) and \(V = \frac{1}{2}v^2 + \frac{1}{2\varepsilon}w^2\):
        $$48b(-\dot{V}) + 81b + 24b I^2 + 12a^2 = 16b\Bigl(v^2 - \frac{9}{4}\Bigr)^2 + 24b(v - I)^2 + 12(2bw - a)^2$$</div>
        <p>Because the right-hand side is an exact sum of squares for every \(b > 0\), every membrane trajectory regardless of stimulation current \(I\) or recovery offset \(a\) is provably trapped inside a compact invariant set—verified by <code>al-id 5 fhn-driven-trapping-sos ≡ true</code> with zero floating-point trust.</p>
        <p>Vary \(I\) from \(0\) to \(0.5\) to trigger the Hopf bifurcation into repetitive action-potential spiking (pink trajectory), always bounded by the exact certified outer envelope.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="synesthesia">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>4. Synthetic Synesthesia, Detector Null-Space &amp; Cognitive Inhibition</h2>
      <span class="mod-tag">neuro/synesthesia.cub · neuro/inhibition.cub · docs/synesthesia.cub</span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
